	(gr_text "Mechanical:\nOutline: 20x25 mm\nSMA jack parallel out of a short side, then resistor and vias to GND on opposite edge.\nStrip with diamonds is exposed copper stripline, 3 mm wide and 20 mm long before mask around resistor's pad, 4.5 mm from short edge.\nThe center diamond is in the geographic middle, then one on each side parallel to the long board side, with between 3 and 5 mm distance.\nThe gap of pours between the stripline hot side and GND, underneath the resistor, is 1.0 mm, but the resistor pads reach into the gap.\nGND Strip with mask along the short side opposite to the SMA connector is 1.6 mm wide.\nThat GND strip is stitched with vias every 1.5 mm except in middle (because the resistor pad is there)\nVia-free area around the GND pad of the resistor is 4mm of the short side of the board, with the resistor pad in the middle of that.\nFab: 1.6 mm board thickness, ENIG\n"
		(at 85 94 0)
		(layer "Cmts.User")
		(uuid "7e6d88e2-2c6d-494d-9fb6-609db9f5f40c")
